children\":\"2. Availability and Data.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"1\",{\"children\":\" MCP Features are unavailable where you have elected Zero Retention Mode or require HIPAA compliance, unless ElevenLabs expressly agrees otherwise in writing. Neither enablement of an MCP Feature nor an exception under Section 4.2 overrides this restriction. You shall not transmit through a Connection data prohibited by the Underlying ElevenLabs Agreement or the ElevenAgents Terms, including Prohibited Data and protected health information. You configure conversation retention, redaction, and related privacy controls described in the Documentation.\"}]]}]}]\n9c:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"25\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"content-element\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontWeight\":\"bold\"},\"children\":\"3. Enablement and Authority.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"1\",{\"children\":\" MCP Features are disabled by default and enabled at workspace level, including by non-administrators. Enablement, acceptance of these ElevenAPI Terms for MCP, and Connections by anyone using your workspace or credentials bind you. You control who may enable features, establish or modify Connections, and approve tool calls. A Connection authorizes the Services and, within granted scopes, MCP Clients to act for you, and their actions are your actions. You represent that you have all rights, consents, and authority necessary for Connections, access to connected systems and data, and ElevenLabs’ transmission, receipt, and processing of that data.\"}]]}]}]\n9d:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"26\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"content-element\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontWeight\":\"bold\"},\"children\":\"4. External MCP Servers.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"1\",{\"children\":\" You are responsible for each External MCP Server, for its operator, and for everything it does in connection with the Services. You shall: (a) vet, configure, and monitor each External MCP Server and its security, availability, lawfulness, and behavior; (b) set tool-approval controls appropriate to the risk of each tool, including requiring approval before a tool writes, deletes, transmits, or otherwise alters data; (c) limit the data exchanged with each External MCP Server to what the relevant tool requires, and remain responsible for that data; (d) guard against prompt injection and other manipulation originating from an External MCP Server, its tool definitions, or the content it returns; (e) secure the credentials, secrets, tokens, headers, and connection details used for each Connection, and use encrypted transport; and (f) promptly notify \"}],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:legal@elevenlabs.io\",\"className\":\"content-element\",\"rel\":\"$undefined\",\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"legal@elevenlabs.io\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"3\",{\"children\":\" of any vulnerability, compromise, or unauthorized access affecting an External MCP Server that is or has been connected to the Services. An operator may change the tools and capabilities its server exposes without notice, and you bear the consequences of any such change.\"}]]}]}]\n9e:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"27\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"content-element\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontWeight\":\"bold\"},\"children\":\"5. MCP Clients.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"1\",{\"children\":\" Connecting an MCP Client to the ElevenLabs MCP Server authorizes that MCP Client to act for you within the scope you grant at sign-in. You are responsible for selecting each MCP Client, for the persons you permit to connect it, for reviewing tool calls before approving them, including destructive actions, and for revoking access when it is no longer required.\"}]]}]}]\n9f:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"28\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\"